==German==
{{wikipedia|lang=de}}

===Etymology===
From {{etym|gmh|de}} {{term|knobelouch|lang=gmh}}, with dissimilation from {{etym|goh|de}} {{term|chlobalouh|lang=goh}}. The latter part of the word is, of course, {{term|Lauch||leek|lang=de}}. The first part originally pertains to {{term|klieben||to cleave|lang=de}}, but was later adapted to the large group of terms for thick objects beginning with ''kn-'' (cf. {{term|Knopf|lang=de}}, {{term|Knoten|lang=de}}, {{term|Knolle|lang=de}}, etc.). The same in {{etym|nl|-}} {{term|knoflook|lang=nl}}.

